a proposal for an urban food truck plot  in downtown las vegas art district  is creating a divide between project  developers and local businesses  reporter kate houston breaking down how  developers want to transform that space  and also the changes that businesses  want to see before that plan moves  forward  project developers want to turn this  vacant area on south casino center and  california avenue  into a bustling food truck lot we want  to bring the culinary arts  to the arts district bringing 10 food  trucks not only 10 food trucks but 10  selective food trucks 10 of the top food  trucks here in las vegas  in december the planning commission  approved the proposal despite  staff recommending against it developers  say the variety of food trucks and open  air concept will help drive more people  into the area  but businesses are concerned about a  lack of sanitation  waste management and how it will look  it's negligent to  the overall well-being and welfare for  not just  the the look of the arts district the  feel of the arts district but  for the well-being of the surrounding  businesses mario enriquez with garagist  which is next to the vacant lot  says the arts district wants to welcome  more small businesses but there needs to  be consistency  holding everybody to the same standards  is what we are all concerned with  and for good reason everybody should be  held to the same standards in order to  promote any given neighborhood or area  project managers say the next steps are  to ensure  everything is in compliance noel  casemiro with great american foodie fest  says he understands the concerns and  they're working to address them  we're going to do our best to create a  win-win situation where everyone is  happy and pleased  and that this food truck concept park  that's going to be in this area is going  to benefit  everyone there instead of impact them in  a negative way  kate houston 8 news now now due to the  pushback from some of those local  businesses there councilwoman olivia  diaz requested the proposal be discussed  before city council and that meeting  will happen we're told now in early  march
 

